From 6b16a91ae091bfc61ce9d3f83c70ef9b50cc9078 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:34:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): one transcript row per remote notice
 when a second profile's sweeper is on the install

A remote notice that woke a turn landed twice: a passive row, then the woken turn's own row (hub: 156 remote
notice_ids in 3 days). Cause: the claim ledger lived in get_hermes_home(), so the example gateways (own profile
homes, sweeping the default chats) claimed in their own ledger. Their wake could not resume the chat
("missing") and wrote the passive row; the Desktop's sweep, in the default ledger, still offered the notice,
woke a turn, and the turn wrote it again. Its own-claim ack was then satisfied by the passive row.

- ledger_path(): one ledger per install (get_default_hermes_root()), so every profile's process sees the claim.
- _claim_notice: a fresh notice whose key is already in the transcript is acked, never offered (no wake).
- Alternation repair: two adjacent user rows of one notice_id keep ONE row, the one with api_content (the
  woken turn's ask-gate block), instead of concatenating the text twice and dropping api_content.

Card t_01a1db370b459fab.
